                                "sense_id": "39b3127c-ba4d-30a6-9190-ba6f528b4379",
                                "text": "The radical element A (“to cut up”), before entering into combination with the coördinate element B (“to sit”), is itself compounded with two nominal elements or element-groups—an instrumentally used stem (F) (“knife”), which may be freely used as the radical element of noun forms but cannot be employed as an absolute noun in its given form, and an objectively used group—(E) + C + d (“black cow or bull”)."
                            }
                        ]
